after a critically acclaimed and wildly  successful origin story Wonder Woman is  heading to 1984 and when she gets there  to find a new foe lying in wait  Wonder Woman director patty Jenkins has  shared the first official image of  actress Kristen Wiig in character on set  of Wonder Woman 1984 portraying the  character Barbara and Minerva aka the  villainous cheetah while it appears to  be a look at Minerva in a normal 80's  lady form it's still cool to see the  character come to life  for the first time ever in a live-action  film even if it does just like a  postcard from a Natural History Museum  with Wiig standing in a dark room  surrounded by exhibits dabbling in a  big-screen super villainy is a new  career move for Wiig who made a name for  herself in comedy with Saturday Night  Live and a Golden Globe nominated turn  in bridesmaids she starred in the reboot  of the Ghostbusters franchise in 2016  but this is a first big foray into the  superhero genre Cheetahs cinematic  backstory is still unclear and in the  comics it varies quite a bit in her  first incarnation as Barbara and Minerva  she's an ambitious archaeologist from a  wealthy family with a flexible moral  compass she gains supernatural powers  while seeking immortality from an  ancient god of plants or by cutting  herself on an ancient dagger or she's  cursed depending on which series you  read in all of our incarnations the  transformation leaves her in a tortured  existence somewhere between human and  feline her natural ambitions are  supercharged by her immense new strength  betweenness inspired casting and the  expected but still unexplained return of  Steve Trevor  Wonder Woman 1984 shaping up to be among  the most interesting movies coming out  of Warner Brothers in DC in the near  future jenkins confirmed on Twitter  earlier this month that despite  sacrificing himself for the safety of  the entire world  Chris Pines Trevor will be in The Wonder  Woman sequel welcome to Wonder Woman  1984 Steve Trevor Jenkins tweeted along  with a photo of pine looking totally 80s  in era appropriate clothes including  what appears to be a Members Only jacket  you remember that Trevor appeared to  have died at the end of the first Wonder  Woman flick which was set in 1917 during  World War one but it looks like he  somehow went on to live for another 67  years and didn't age a single day is  this Steve Trevor a relative of the  original Steve Trevor is there some sort  of time travel in play as he  to stylish hallucination we'll have to  wait and find out as a bonus treat  Wonder Woman herself actress gal gadot  also took to Twitter recently to share a  photo from the sequel in it diana has  seen staring at a wall of screens most  of which display period-appropriate  shapes colors and stock images but one  shows actor Larry Hagman as jr. Ewing on  the 1980s primetime soap opera Dallas  from the original film's performance we  already know the team behind this can  make an excellent superhero flick Wonder  Woman broke a ton of Records in the  summer of 2017 becoming the  highest-grossing DC extended universe  film ever at the domestic box office the  most commercially successful superhero  origin story movie in history and the  top earning live-action film directed by  a woman in sotol the flick took home 821  million dollars worldwide and sits  certified fresh' with a 92 percent  critical score and an 88% audience  rating on Rotten Tomatoes speaking with  Entertainment Tonight Jenkins promised  that the sequel will be a completely  fresh experience compared to its  predecessor it's not Wonder Woman to to  us is an entirely new adventure when the  woman 1984 will be out in theaters on  November 1st 2019 thanks for watching  click the loop icon to subscribe to our  YouTube channel plus check out all this  cool stuff we do love to  [Music]
 

